title: Scale in the Scene view
intro: Drag the square handles on the selection's corners and edges to scale it, right in the Scene view.
project: TopDown | Scene Scale

create: Sprite
rename: Rug
set: Transform.Position = 7, 1, 0
set: Sprite.Tint = #7E2553
deselect
create: Sprite
rename: Lamp
set: Transform.Position = 9.5, 1, 0
set: Sprite.Size = 0.5, 0.5
set: Sprite.Tint = #FFEC27

chapter: Scale handles | Drag an edge or a corner
select: Rug
look: 8.5, 1.5, 3.5
say: Here's a rug to lay in the dungeon. Making it bigger used to mean typing numbers into the Scale field.
explain: handle:right | Scale handles | Now the selection has square handles on its corners and edges. An edge stretches it one way.
scale: Ctrl+right = 3
expectvalue: Rug.Transform.Scale.X = 3
expectvalue: Rug.Transform.Scale.Y = 1
explain: field:Transform.Scale | Snapped | Holding control snaps the scale to tenths, so this is exactly three wide.
explain: handle:top-right | Corners | A corner scales both ways at once. Holding shift keeps the proportions.
scale: Ctrl+Shift+top-right = 0.5
expectvalue: Rug.Transform.Scale.X = 1.5
expectvalue: Rug.Transform.Scale.Y = 0.5
say: Without control it scales freely, landing on hundredths. Each drag is one step to undo.
key: Ctrl+Z
expectvalue: Rug.Transform.Scale.X = 3

chapter: Scaling several | Around the one picked last
select: Lamp
select: Ctrl+Rug
expectselected: Lamp, Rug
say: With several selected, the handles sit on the one picked last, here the rug.
scale: Ctrl+Shift+top-right = 2
expectvalue: Rug.Transform.Scale.X = 6
expectvalue: Lamp.Transform.Scale.X = 2
expectat: Lamp = 12, 1
explain: world:3.5, 3, 12.8, -1 | Grown together | Everything grows around the rug together: the lamp doubled too, and moved out to stay beside it.
key: Ctrl+Z
expectat: Lamp = 9.5, 1
say: And one undo puts them both back.
